			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b27b4691-22e2-47d5-a3c1-cdaf874224b7")
	)
	(text "1. U3 SN65HVD230 — 3.3 V CAN transceiver, 500 kbit/s (CANopen); C8 100 nF at VCC.\n   Rs (pin 8) → R16 0 Ω → GND = high-speed mode. Fit ≈ 10 kΩ instead of R16 for slower,\n   lower-EMI edges (+≈ 50 ns, negligible at 500 kbit/s). Vref (pin 5) unused.\n   D (pin 1): internal 100 kΩ pull-up + R15 10 kΩ to +3V3 → CAN_TX idles recessive while\n   the MCU is in reset, blank or being flashed.\n   Bus pins rated −4…+16 V, common mode −2…+7 V; no TXD time-out (carrier rule 9).\n\n2. Bus termination — 120 Ω at each physical bus end → 60 Ω total\n   JP1 OPEN by default; bridge only on a module at a bus end.\n   R7 0603 (100 mW): 33 mW typ (VOD 2 V), 75 mW worst (VOD 3 V, bus held dominant) OK\n   Check: power off, CANH–CANL ≈ 60 Ω on a correctly terminated bus.\n\n3. D1 NUP2105L — dual-line CAN ESD protector between U3 and the fingers (stand-off 24 V,\n   breakdown ≥ 26.2 V, 26–30 pF). It absorbs ESD / fast surges only. It does NOT protect U3\n   against a DC fault between +16 V and +26 V, or below −4 V → carrier rule 9.\n\n4. PCB impedance — JLC04081H-3313 (F.Cu over In1 GND, prepreg 0.0994 mm, εr 4.1)\n   CAN  0.10 / 0.25 mm pair → ≈ 118 Ω diff   (bus 120 Ω)\n   USB  0.15 / 0.13 mm pair → ≈ 90 Ω diff    (USB wired to fingers 23/25, not used)\n   (Hammerstad–Jensen; verify with JLCPCB's impedance calculator before ordering.)\n\n5. M.2 2242 B-key card edge: custom pinout, odd fingers top / even fingers bottom;\n   see the finger map tables. Card: 0.8 mm, ENIG, bevelled gold fingers.\n   Carrier spec: MES4-CIF (CARRIER_INTERFACE.md)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 31.75 220.345 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b8517cb1-63c1-4eb4-bd03-cc8e6b467f70")
	)
